HST Office: count a banner display once the card stood one second in a visible window.

Owner decision (2026-11-12): banner displays are counted, per local day and banner id (docs/BANNERS.md,
"Display counting").

- sfx2/source/notebookbar/HstRibbonBanner.{hxx,cxx}: when the delivered card has another id than the
  last card change, a one-second main-thread timer checks that the card is drawn in view: the slot is
  really visible, the image is decoded and the work window is not minimized, at the start and at the
  end of the second. Not in view: it checks again every second while the slot is shown (a hidden slot
  restarts the second when it is placed again). The same card is counted once until the card changes;
  the compact/wide switch and rescaling, which deliver the same id again, do not count. The count is a
  call of org.hst.office.BannerFeed with NamedValue("Shown", id) on a short worker thread
  (ShownThread), so the UI thread never calls Python; nothing is posted back and failures are ignored.
  The last worker is joined on dispose like the click worker.

